hadiths[200]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8075","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said wine was made unlawful in three stages. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Madinah, people drank wine and consumed gambling gains, so Allah sent down the verse of al-Baqarah 219, and people said nothing was yet made unlawful. Then a Muhajir led Maghrib and confused the recitation, so Allah sent down the verse commanding believers not to approach prayer while drunk, and people drank only until sober for prayer. Then Allah sent down al-Maidah 90, and they said we stop, our Lord, and when asked about those killed or dead who had drunk, Allah sent down al-Maidah 93. > **""If it had been made unlawful upon them, they would have left it just as you have left it.""**"
"8076","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, said he was serving the people figs and raisins mixed together, and a man called Abu Bakr drank and recited poetry about greeting Umm Bakr and denying resurrection. While they were drinking, a Muslim entered and said Allah had sent down the prohibition of wine, so they spilled the vessel and overturned it, then went out to find the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, standing on the pulpit repeating the verse of al-Maidah 91. > **""Satan only wants to cause enmity and hatred among you through wine and gambling and to hinder you from remembrance of Allah and prayer, so will you stop.""**"
"8077","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said he was passing the cup among Abu Talhah, Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, Muadh ibn Jabal, Suhayl ibn Bayda and Abu Dujanah, may Allah be pleased with them, until their heads tilted, when a caller announced wine had been made unlawful. No one entered or left, but they poured out the drink, broke the jugs, some performed ablution and some bathed, applied perfume of Umm Sulaym, and went to the mosque where the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited al-Maidah 90 to 91. A man asked about those who died drinking it, so Allah sent down al-Maidah 93, and Anas affirmed he heard it directly and the Companions never lied nor knew lying. > **""O you who believe, wine, gambling, idols and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them that you may succeed, until: so will you stop.""**"
"8078","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, said when the prohibition of wine came down, he entered upon companions with wine before them, struck it with his foot, and told them to go to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for the prohibition had come down. He then narrated the report."
"8079","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said when wine was made unlawful, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walked to one another saying wine had been made unlawful and made equal to shirk."
"8080","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade six things: domestic donkeys, wine, gambling, flutes, the hand-drum, and the kubah drum. Ibn Abbas added that every intoxicant is unlawful. > **""Every intoxicant is unlawful.""**"
"8081","Abu al-Darda or Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the first thing his Lord forbade him after worship of idols was drinking wine and quarreling with men. > **""The first thing my Lord forbade me after worship of idols was drinking wine and quarreling with men.""**"
"8082","Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said among the first things his Lord entrusted to him and forbade him after worship of idols and drinking wine was quarreling with men. > **""Among the first things my Lord entrusted to me and forbade me after worship of idols and drinking wine was quarreling with men.""**"
"8083","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said wine is unlawful in itself, little of it and much, and whatever intoxicates from any drink."
"8084","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him to bring a knife, had it sharpened, then went with his Companions to the markets of Madinah where wineskins had been brought from Syria. He took the knife and cut open what was there in his presence, then ordered Ibn Umar with helpers to go through all markets and cut every wineskin, and he left none uncut. > **""Come to me with it in the morning.""**"
"8085","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said in another narration that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went to the Mirbad with him on his right, then Abu Bakr came and Ibn Umar yielded, then Umar came and he yielded, until they reached wineskins of wine. The Prophet called for the knife, a word Ibn Umar only learned that day, and ordered the skins cut. > **""Bring me the knife.""**"
"8086","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, said on the day of the conquest of Makkah the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, poured out the wine and broke its jars."
"8087","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that a man of Thaqif gifted the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a waterskin of wine after wine had been made unlawful, so the Prophet ordered it split open. The full report was mentioned earlier under the price of wine. > **""Pour it out and cut it open.""**"
"8088","Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said his Lord, blessed and exalted, made unlawful upon him wine, the kubah drum and the qinnin lute, and warned against ghubayra, for it is a third of the wine of the world. > **""My Lord has made wine, the kubah and the qinnin unlawful upon me, and beware of ghubayra, for it is a third of the wine of the world.""**"
"8089","Umm Habibah daughter of Abu Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, learned prayer and laws, then asked about a drink of wheat and barley. He asked if it was ghubayra, they said yes, and three times he told them not to taste it, and when they said they would not leave it, he commanded striking the neck of whoever did not leave it. > **""Is it ghubayra. Do not taste it. Whoever does not leave it, strike his neck.""**"
"8090","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said their wine in those days was fadikh, and when it was made unlawful, it was none other than the fadikh people make."
"8091","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, raised to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that whoever dies with the smell of fadikh in his belly, Allah will disgrace him before all witnesses on the Day of Resurrection. > **""Whoever dies with the smell of fadikh in his belly, Allah will disgrace him before all witnesses on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8092","Maqil ibn Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, when asked about drinks, said they were in Madinah, rich in dates, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fadikh."
"8093","In another narration, Maqil poured it out saying this is the last covenant with wine."
"8094","Abu Talhah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the two mixtures. > **""Do not mix two kinds together.""**"
"8095","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to soak dates alone and unripe dates alone, and said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded soaking each one separately. > **""Soak each one of them separately.""**"
"8096","Abu Usayd, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade combining dates and raisins. > **""Do not combine dates and raisins.""**"
"8097","Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his mother who prayed both qiblahs with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said she heard the Prophet forbid dates and raisins together and command soaking each one alone. > **""Soak each one of them alone.""**"
"8098","Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his mother who prayed both qiblahs, may Allah be pleased with her, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said not to make nabidh of dates and raisins together, but each one separately. > **""Do not make nabidh of dates and raisins together, and make nabidh of each one separately.""**"
"8099","Umm Mabad, may Allah be pleased with her, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid the two mixtures. Asked what they are, it was said dates and raisins. Umm Mughith, grandmother of Rabiah, had prayed both qiblahs in his time. > **""Dates and raisins.""**"
"8100","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the first thing overturned of Islam, as a vessel is overturned, will be over a drink called tila. > **""The first thing overturned of Islam, as a vessel is overturned, will be over a drink called tila.""**"
"8101","Al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful said he asked Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, about vessels, and he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade pitched vessels and said every intoxicant is unlawful. Asked about muqayyar, lead and glass, he permitted them, said leave doubt for certainty, that drunkenness is unlawful, little and much, and that wine comes from grapes, dates, honey, wheat, barley and corn, whatever ferments thereof is wine. > **""Every intoxicant is unlawful. Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt. Little and much of what intoxicates is unlawful.""**"
"8102","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about a Yemeni drink called bit and mizr, and said whatever intoxicates is unlawful. > **""Whatever intoxicates is unlawful.""**"
"8103","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, said he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid what is made in vessels, and that every intoxicant is unlawful. > **""Every intoxicant is unlawful.""**"
"8104","Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say every intoxicant is unlawful. > **""Every intoxicant is unlawful.""**"
"8105","Qurrah ibn Iyas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said every intoxicant is unlawful. > **""Every intoxicant is unlawful.""**"
"8106","Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with them, said he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say every intoxicant is wine and every intoxicant is unlawful. > **""Every intoxicant is wine and every intoxicant is unlawful.""**"
"8107","Abdullah ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said his community will drink wine in later times calling it by another name. > **""My community will drink wine in later times calling it by another name.""**"
"8108","Maymunah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said not to make nabidh in gourds, jars or pitched vessels, and every drink that intoxicates is unlawful. More reports of this chapter will come under vessels. > **""Do not make nabidh in gourds, jars or pitched vessels, and every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.""**"
"8109","Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful. > **""Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful.""**"
"8110","Khawwat ibn Jubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful. > **""Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful.""**"
"8111","Maqil ibn Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, said they were in Madinah rich in fruit, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fadikh to them. A man asked about giving nabidh to a weak old woman who ate no food, and Maqil forbade him."
"8112","Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, may Allah be pleased with him, said he brought jar nabidh to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked about it, and the Prophet forbade it to him, so he took the jar and broke it. > **""It is forbidden.""**"
"8113","Abu Ishaq freedman of Banu Hashim reported they disputed over what may be used for nabidh, especially gourds, and Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, passing by, said he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid every pitched vessel used for nabidh, so the gourd was rejected. > **""I heard the Messenger of Allah forbid every pitched vessel used for nabidh.""**"
"8114","Samurah ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood, preached, and forbade gourds and pitched vessels. > **""Do not use gourds or pitched vessels.""**"
"8115","Maymunah wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reported that he said not to make nabidh in gourds, pitched vessels, hollowed stumps or jars, and every intoxicant is unlawful. > **""Do not make nabidh in gourds, pitched vessels, hollowed stumps or jars, and every intoxicant is unlawful.""**"
"8116","Abu Shimr al-Dubai said he heard Aidh ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, forbid gourds, hantam jars, pitched vessels and hollowed stumps, and when asked if from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said yes."
"8117","Al-Fudayl ibn Yazid al-Raqashi said they were with Abdullah ibn Maqil discussing drinks, and Ibn Maqil said wine is unlawful and he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid gourds, hantam and pitched vessels. Asked what hantam is, he said green and white jars, and muzaffat is every pitch-coated skin or otherwise. In another narration hollowed stumps were added, and the narrator bought a waterskin kept hanging in his house. > **""I heard the Messenger of Allah forbid gourds, hantam and pitched vessels.""**"
"8118","Abdullah ibn Jabir al-Abdi said he was with his father among the delegation of Abd al-Qays to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who forbade drinking in the vessels they had heard of: gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps and pitched vessels. > **""Do not drink in gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps or pitched vessels.""**"
"8119","Duljah ibn Qays reported that al-Hakam al-Ghifari said to a man, do you remember the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbidding gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps and pitch-coated vessels. He said yes, and al-Hakam said and I bear witness."
"8120","In another narration, al-Hakam al-Ghifari said to a man, do you remember when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade hollowed stumps and pitch-coated vessels or one of them, and gourds and hantam. He said yes, and al-Hakam said and I bear witness to that."
"8121","Duljah ibn Qays reported that a man said to al-Hakam al-Ghifari, do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade gourds and hantam. He said yes, and the other said and I bear witness to that."
"8122","Suhayrah daughter of Jayfar said they performed Hajj, returned to Madinah, entered upon Safiyyah daughter of Huyayy, may Allah be pleased with her, with Kufan women who asked about women's matters, menstruation, then jar nabidh. Safiyyah said Iraqis ask too much about it, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade jar nabidh, and a woman may cook her dates, rub them, strain them, put them in her waterskin tied shut, and drink and serve her husband when sweet. > **""The Messenger of Allah forbade jar nabidh. Cook your dates, strain them, tie them in your waterskin, and drink when sweet.""**"
"8123","Shihab ibn Abbad heard men of Abd al-Qays say they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who rejoiced at them. Al-Ashajj said their land was heavy and unhealthy, and without these drinks their colors changed and bellies swelled. The Prophet told them not to drink in gourds, hantam or hollowed stumps, but each should drink from a skin tied at its mouth. When al-Ashajj begged permission with cupped hands, the Prophet warned if permitted that much they would drink that much with outspread hands. > **""Do not drink in gourds, hantam or hollowed stumps, and let each of you drink from a skin tied at its mouth.""**"
"8124","Abu al-Qamus Zayd ibn Ali reported from a delegate of Abd al-Qays that they gifted a bag of choice dates, the Prophet returned a date to its place, told them to convey it to the family of Muhammad, then when asked about drinks said not to drink in gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps or pitched vessels, but in lawful tied vessels. Asked how he knew these vessels, he swore by Hajar, its pride, entering it and seizing its key. He stood toward the qiblah praying for Abd al-Qays and praising them as the best of the East. > **""Do not drink in gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps or pitched vessels. Drink in lawful tied vessels. O Allah, forgive Abd al-Qays, who submitted willingly. The best of the East are Abd al-Qays.""**"
"8125","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade hollowed stumps, gourds and pitched vessels, and said to drink only from what has a tie. People made camel skins with sheep-neck openings, and when told, he said to drink only from what is tied above. > **""Do not drink except from what has a tie.""**"
"8126","Al-Ashath ibn Umayr al-Abdi, from his father, said the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and before leaving were told to ask about nabidh. They said their land was unhealthy and only drink helped them. Asked what and in what, they said nabidh in hollowed stumps, and he thrice told them not to drink in hollowed stumps, warning a man may strike his cousin a blow lame till Resurrection. They laughed, admitting it had already happened among them. > **""Do not drink in hollowed stumps, lest a man among you strike his cousin a blow lame till the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8127","Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade gourds, hantam and jars. > **""Do not use gourds, hantam or jars.""**"
"8128","Qatadah said he asked Anas about jar nabidh, and Anas said he heard nothing from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about it, though Anas disliked it."
"8129","Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, said he awaited the breaking of the fast of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, brought jar nabidh, and when brought to his mouth it fizzed, so he ordered striking it against the wall, for it is the drink of one who disbelieves in Allah and the Last Day. > **""Strike it against the wall, for this is the drink of one who does not believe in Allah nor the Last Day.""**"
"8130","Amr ibn Sufyan said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told him to forbid jar nabidh, for it is unlawful from Allah and His Messenger. > **""Forbid jar nabidh, for it is unlawful from Allah and His Messenger.""**"
"8131","Amr ibn Sufyan said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told him to forbid his people jar nabidh, for it is unlawful from Allah and His Messenger. > **""Forbid your people jar nabidh, for it is unlawful from Allah and His Messenger.""**"
"8132","Safwan ibn al-Muattal, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him to announce not to make nabidh in jars. > **""Do not make nabidh in jars.""**"
"8133","Abu al-Aliyah said he asked Abu Said about vessels, and he said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade vessels except tied waterskins. > **""Do not use vessels except what is tied of waterskins.""**"
"8134","Abu Hajib, from a Ghifari Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, reported that the Prophet forbade pitch-coated, hollowed, gourd and hantam vessels. > **""Do not use pitch-coated, hollowed, gourd or hantam vessels.""**"
"8135","Zayd ibn Arqam and Qarazah ibn Kab, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade gourds, pitched vessels and hollowed stumps. > **""Do not use gourds, pitched vessels or hollowed stumps.""**"
"8136","Abu Khayrah al-Subahi said he was among forty delegates to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who forbade gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps and pitch-coated vessels, then ordered arak sticks for siwak. When they said they had herbs sufficing them, he raised his hands praying forgiveness for Abd al-Qays who submitted willingly. > **""Use these for siwak. O Allah, forgive Abd al-Qays, who submitted willingly without aversion.""**"
"8137","Abu Bakrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said they were forbidden gourds, pitched vessels and hollowed stumps."
"8138","Al-Numan ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with them, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said not to drink in hollowed stumps or pitched vessels. > **""Do not drink in hollowed stumps or pitched vessels.""**"
"8139","Umm Mabad freedwoman of Qarazah said gourds are pumpkins the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade, hantam are jars of non-Arab lands he forbade, and naqir are hollowed green palm stumps he forbade. Maqil ibn Yasar already clarified this with sound chain, so no need for this."
"8140","Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, may Allah be pleased with him, said he witnessed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he forbade jar nabidh, and witnessed him when he permitted it, saying avoid intoxicants. > **""Avoid intoxicants.""**"
"8141","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said when the delegation of Abd al-Qays turned away, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said every person is accountable for himself, let each people make nabidh as they wish. > **""Every person is accountable for himself. Let each people make nabidh as they wish.""**"
"8142","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said he witnessed the Abd al-Qays delegation when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade hantam, gourds, pitched and hollowed vessels. A man said people have no vessels, and the Prophet, pitying them, said drink it when sweet and leave it when spoiled. > **""Drink it when sweet, and when spoiled leave it.""**"
"8143","Al-Rasim reported they came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who forbade vessels, then came again complaining their land was unhealthy, and he said drink in whatever you wish, whoever ties his skin bears his sin. > **""Drink in whatever you wish. Whoever ties his waterskin bears his sin.""**"
"8144","Yahya ibn Ghassan, from his father in the Abd al-Qays delegation, said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade these vessels, they abstained and suffered, then returned next year complaining, and he said make nabidh in whatever you wish and do not drink intoxicants, whoever ties his skin bears his sin. > **""Make nabidh in whatever you wish, and do not drink intoxicants. Whoever ties his waterskin bears his sin.""**"
"8145","Ibn al-Rasibi, from his learned father of Hajar, said he went with charity to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who forbade nabidh in these vessels. They returned to hot Tihamah, suffered, came next year and complained of hardship, so he said go, drink in whatever you wish, do not drink intoxicants, whoever ties his skin bears his sin. > **""Go and drink in whatever you wish, and do not drink intoxicants. Whoever ties his waterskin bears his sin.""**"
"8146","Asim reported from Mundhir Abu Hassan, from Samurah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted nabidh after having forbidden it. > **""I have permitted nabidh after having forbidden it.""**"
"8147","Suhar al-Abdi, may Allah be pleased with him, said he asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for permission to make nabidh in a jar, and he permitted it. > **""I permit you to make nabidh in a jar.""**"
"8148","Al-Ashajj al-Asri said he came with Abd al-Qays riders, tethered mounts while others rushed in travel clothes, then changed before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said he has two traits loved by Allah and His Messenger: forbearance and deliberation. Asked if innate or acquired, the Prophet said innate, so he praised Allah. They complained their faces changed after vessels were forbidden in unhealthy land, and the Prophet said vessels neither forbid nor permit, but every intoxicant is unlawful, lest men drink till veins rage, boast, and one strike his cousin with a sword leaving him lame, and the lame victim stood among them. > **""In you are two traits loved by Allah and His Messenger: forbearance and deliberation. Vessels neither forbid nor permit, but every intoxicant is unlawful.""**"
"8149","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said she used to make nabidh for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a green jar."
"8150","Abu Bakrah, may Allah be pleased with him, used to have nabidh made for him in a green jar. Abu Barzah returned from absence, visited his house, missed him, asked his wife what was in the jar, and wished it placed in a waterskin, which she did. When Abu Bakrah returned and learned this, he refused to drink from it, saying putting wine in a skin would not make it lawful nor honey in a jar unlawful, for they knew what was forbidden: gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps and pitched vessels. He explained Thaqif hollowed gourds filled with grape clusters warmed till fermented dead, Yamamah hollowed palm stumps filled with ripe dates left till fermented, hantam were red jars wine came in, and pitched vessels contain tar. > **""We were forbidden gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps and pitched vessels.""**"
"8151","Talq ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said they sat with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when Abd al-Qays came. He asked why their colors yellowed, bellies swelled and veins showed. They said their leader asked about a suitable drink and he forbade it, while their land was unhealthy, so he said drink whatever you wish. > **""Drink whatever you wish.""**"
"8152","Abu Malik al-Ashjai, may Allah be pleased with him, said nabidh was made for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a stone basin."
"8153","Umayr ibn Muslim said a green jar containing camphor was gifted to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he divided among Muhajirun and Ansar, and told Umm Sulaym, may Allah be pleased with her, to make nabidh for them in it. > **""O Umm Sulaym, make nabidh for us in it.""**"
"8154","Qurrah ibn Iyas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when asked about vessels, said vessels forbid nothing, so make nabidh in whatever you wish but avoid every intoxicant. > **""Vessels forbid nothing. Make nabidh in whatever you wish and avoid every intoxicant.""**"
"8155","Shaqiq ibn Salamah reported from Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, that he gave him nabidh in a green jar, and Abu Wail said he had seen that jar."
"8156","Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami said he asked al-Hasan about nabidh, who said drink only from what is tied. His son said had it not reached them that Ibn Masud drank with them from a green jar. He said yes indeed."
"8157","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade visiting graves, sacrificial meat beyond three days, and nabidh in hollowed stumps, gourds and pitched vessels. Then he said he had forbidden three things but changed them: visit graves for they soften hearts, tear eyes and remind of Hereafter without foul speech; keep sacrificial meat as you wish for guests and absent ones; and drink in whatever vessels but no intoxicants, whoever ties his skin bears his sin. > **""I forbade you three things, then I changed them. Visit graves, keep what you wish, drink in whatever you wish but do not drink intoxicants. Whoever ties his waterskin bears his sin.""**"
"8158","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade these vessels, gourds, hantam, hollowed stumps and pitched vessels, then permitted them saying drink in whatever you wish but avoid every intoxicant. He also forbade grave visits then said visit them for admonition. > **""Drink in whatever you wish and avoid every intoxicant. Visit graves, for in them is admonition.""**"
"8159","Sharahil said he asked Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, about a man taking a cluster, pressing and drinking it. He said no harm, and when drunk said its drinking is lawful and its sale lawful."
"8160","Suhar ibn Sakhr al-Abdi told the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that their land had much bread and greens and they drank nabidh with it, and the Prophet said drink of it what does not remove mind and wealth. > **""Drink of it what does not remove mind and wealth.""**"
"8161","Abdullah ibn Abi al-Shikhkhir said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade drinks, and when told they are necessary, said drink what does not corrupt your minds nor consume your wealth. > **""Drink what does not corrupt your minds nor consume your wealth.""**"
"8162","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought nabidh and drank from it."
"8163","Al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a vessel of nabidh, poured water over it till it overflowed, then drank from it."
"8164","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not drink nabidh beyond three days."
"8165","Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, said nabidh was made overnight for the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he drank the next day, the following night, and that night till the third day, then withheld."
"8166","Al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wadaah said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, circumambulated on a hot day, thirsted, asked for drink, and a man brought a great cup of this raisin drink. The Prophet brought it to his mouth, found a strong odor, disliked and returned it."
"8167","Suhar ibn al-Abbas reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, O Suhar, make your drink good and serve your neighbor. > **""O Suhar, make your drink good and serve your neighbor.""**"
"8168","Umm Mabad freedwoman of Qarazah said she used to serve men among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, including Zayd ibn Arqam and Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with them."
"8169","Said ibn Shubah, from his father from his grandfather, said he saw Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, drinking tila."
"8170","Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah said the nabidh of Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, was sweet, lips stuck from it."
"8171","Thumamah ibn Abdullah ibn Anas said he accompanied his grandfather Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, thirty years and never saw him drink nabidh at all."
"8172","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said wine is the mother of obscenities and greatest of major sins; whoever drinks it falls upon his mother, maternal aunt and paternal aunt. > **""Wine is the mother of obscenities and the greatest of major sins. Whoever drinks it falls upon his mother, maternal aunt and paternal aunt.""**"
"8173","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that Abu Bakr, Umar and Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, after the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, discussed the greatest major sin without knowledge, and sent him to Abdullah ibn Amr, who said the greatest is drinking wine. They denied it and confronted him, and he told them the Prophet said a king of Israel gave a man choice between wine, killing a boy, eating pork, or being killed. He chose wine, then committed all. The Prophet added no drinker has prayer accepted forty nights, if any remains in his bladder paradise is forbidden him, and dying within forty dies a jahili death. > **""No one drinks it but prayer is not accepted for forty nights. If he dies with any in his bladder, paradise is forbidden him, and if he dies within forty he dies a jahili death.""**"
"8174","Attab ibn Amir said he was with Abdullah ibn Amr in the Hijr at Makkah when asked about wine. Ibn Amr sent the asker to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who answered it is the greatest of major sins and mother of obscenities; whoever drinks wine abandons prayer and falls upon mother, maternal aunt and paternal aunt. > **""It is the greatest of major sins and the mother of obscenities. Whoever drinks wine abandons prayer and falls upon his mother, maternal aunt and paternal aunt.""**"
"8175","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say when Allah sent Adam down, angels objected, claimed greater obedience, and Allah sent Harut and Marut down. Al-Zuhrah appeared as a beautiful woman, demanded shirk, they refused, then she returned with a boy demanding wine, they drank, got drunk, fell upon her, killed the boy, then admitted all when sober, and chose torment of this world over the Hereafter. > **""When they drank they got drunk, fell upon her and killed the boy, so they chose the torment of this world.""**"
"8176","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks wine has no prayer accepted forty nights, if he repents Allah turns to him, if he repeats likewise, and on the third or fourth repetition Allah must give him tinat al-khabal to drink. Asked what it is, he said the pus of Hell's people. > **""Whoever drinks wine has no prayer accepted for forty nights. If he repeats, Allah must give him tinat al-khabal to drink: the pus of Hell's people.""**"
"8177","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks wine till drunk has no prayer accepted forty nights, likewise the second, and on the third or fourth, if he repents Allah will not turn to him, and Allah must give him ayn khabal, the pus of Hell's people. > **""Whoever drinks wine till drunk has no prayer accepted for forty nights. On the third or fourth, Allah must give him ayn khabal to drink: the pus of Hell's people.""**"
"8178","Asma daughter of Yazid, may Allah be pleased with her, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say whoever drinks wine, Allah is displeased with him forty nights; if he dies he dies a disbeliever, if he repents Allah turns to him, if he repeats Allah must give him tinat al-khabal, the pus of Hell's people. > **""Whoever drinks wine, Allah is displeased with him for forty nights. If he repeats, Allah must give him tinat al-khabal: the pus of Hell's people.""**"
"8179","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Allah sent him as mercy and guidance, commanding destruction of flutes, lutes, stringed instruments and idols of Jahiliyyah. His Lord swore none of His servants drinks a sip of wine but he will give him boiling Hell in its place, punished or forgiven, none gives it to a small child but likewise, and none leaves it from fear of Him but he will give it in the enclosure of Holiness. > **""Allah sent me as mercy and guidance and commanded me to destroy flutes, lutes and idols. None drinks a sip of wine but I give him boiling Hell in its place, and none leaves it from fear of Me but I give him drink in the enclosure of Holiness.""**"
"8180","In another narration, none gives it to a small weak Muslim child but he will be given pus to drink. > **""None gives it to a small weak Muslim child but he will be given pus to drink.""**"
"8181","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever abandons prayer drunk once, it is as if he owned the world and was stripped of it, and whoever does so four times, Allah must give him tinat al-khabal, the pus of Hell's people. > **""Whoever abandons prayer drunk once, it is as if he owned the world and was stripped of it. Whoever does so four times, Allah must give him tinat al-khabal: the pus of Hell's people.""**"
"8182","Talq ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said he sat with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when Suhar of Abd al-Qays asked about a drink from their fruits. The Prophet turned away till asked three times and finished prayer, then asked who asks about intoxicants, commanding not to drink it nor serve a Muslim brother, swearing none drinks seeking drunken pleasure but Allah will give him wine on Resurrection Day. > **""Who asks about intoxicants. Do not drink it nor serve your Muslim brother it. None drinks seeking drunken pleasure but Allah will give him wine on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8183","Abu Tamim al-Jayshani heard Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah al-Ansari in Egypt say he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, warn whoever lies upon him deliberately to take a seat in Fire, and whoever drinks wine comes thirsty on Resurrection, every intoxicant is wine, beware ghubayra. Then he heard Abdullah ibn Amr say the same, differing only in house or seat. > **""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take a seat in Fire. Whoever drinks wine comes thirsty on the Day of Resurrection. Every intoxicant is wine, and beware of ghubayra.""**"
"8184","Iyad ibn Ghanm, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say whoever drinks wine has no prayer accepted forty days, if he dies then to Fire, if he repents Allah accepts, likewise the second, and on the third or fourth Allah must give him radghat al-khabal, the pus of Hell's people. > **""Whoever drinks wine has no prayer accepted for forty days. On the third or fourth, Allah must give him radghat al-khabal: the pus of Hell's people.""**"
"8185","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks till the mind Allah gave him departs has entered a gate of major sins. > **""Whoever drinks till the mind Allah gave him departs has entered a gate of major sins.""**"
"8186","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever gets drunk from wine has no prayer accepted forty days, and if he dies therein he is like an idol worshiper. > **""Whoever gets drunk from wine has no prayer accepted for forty days, and if he dies therein he is like an idol worshiper.""**"
"8187","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the wine drinker is like an idol worshiper. > **""The wine drinker is like an idol worshiper.""**"
"8188","Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said know every intoxicant is unlawful; Allah has covenanted for whoever drinks an intoxicant to give him tinat al-khabal. > **""Know every intoxicant is unlawful. Allah has covenanted for whoever drinks an intoxicant to give him tinat al-khabal.""**"
"8189","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks wine, Allah will give him boiling Hell to drink. > **""Whoever drinks wine, Allah will give him boiling Hell to drink.""**"
"8190","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks wine is impure forty days, if he repents Allah turns to him, likewise the second and third, and on the fourth Allah must give him radghat al-khabal. Asked what it is, he said the fat and pus of Hell's people. > **""Whoever drinks wine is impure for forty days. On the fourth, Allah must give him radghat al-khabal: the fat and pus of Hell's people.""**"
"8191","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say whoever drinks a sip of wine, Allah accepts neither obligatory nor voluntary deeds for three days; whoever drinks a cup, Allah accepts nothing for forty mornings; and the addict, Allah must give him nahr al-khabal, the pus of Hell's people. > **""Whoever drinks a sip of wine, Allah accepts neither obligatory nor voluntary deeds for three days. Whoever drinks a cup, nothing is accepted for forty mornings. The addict, Allah must give him nahr al-khabal: the pus of Hell's people.""**"
"8192","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks wine into his belly has no prayer accepted for seven days, if he dies therein he dies a disbeliever; if it removes his mind from any duty, no prayer is accepted forty days, and dying therein is dying a disbeliever. > **""Whoever drinks wine into his belly has no prayer accepted for seven days. If it removes his mind from any duty, no prayer is accepted for forty days.""**"
"8193","Al-Saib ibn Yazid, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks any intoxicant, Allah accepts no prayer from him for forty days. > **""Whoever drinks any intoxicant, Allah accepts no prayer from him for forty days.""**"
"8194","Al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman said he sat with Muawiyah when he summoned Abdullah ibn Amr about reports, threatening exile from Syria. Ibn Amr said were it not for dependents he would not stay an hour, affirmed he would not lie upon the Prophet, recalled whoever lies upon him takes a seat in Fire, and recalled about wine: whoever places it on his palm has no supplication accepted, whoever persists is given khabal, a valley in Hell. Muawiyah nearly believed him then fell silent. > **""Whoever lies upon me, let him take his seat in Fire. Whoever places wine on his palm has no supplication accepted, and whoever persists is given khabal, a valley in Hell.""**"
"8195","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said wine is the mother of obscenities; whoever drinks it has no prayer accepted forty days, and if he dies with it in his belly he dies a jahili death. > **""Wine is the mother of obscenities. Whoever drinks it has no prayer accepted for forty days, and if he dies with it in his belly he dies a jahili death.""**"
"8196","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks wine, the light of faith leaves his belly. > **""Whoever drinks wine, the light of faith leaves his belly.""**"
"8197","Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said three are not approached by angels: the drunk, one perfumed with saffron, and the menstruating woman or junub. > **""Three are not approached by angels: the drunk, one perfumed with saffron, and the menstruating woman or junub.""**"
"8198","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said three are not approached by angels: the junub, the drunk, and one perfumed with khaluq. > **""Three are not approached by angels: the junub, the drunk, and one perfumed with khaluq.""**"
"8199","Umar ibn Shaybah, from his father, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said flushing of the face from nabidh scatters good deeds. > **""Flushing of the face from nabidh scatters good deeds.""**"
"8200","Ibrahim said Ibn Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, said do not give your children wine, for they were born upon fitrah; do you give them what is unlawful for them. Its sin is upon whoever gives them, for Allah placed no cure in what He forbade you."
"8201","Abdullah said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed wine, its drinker, server, presser, one for whom pressed, carrier, one to whom carried, seller, buyer and consumer of its price. Similar reports came earlier under the price of wine. > **""Allah has cursed wine, its drinker, server, presser, carrier, seller, buyer and consumer of its price.""**"
"8202","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say Jibril, peace be upon him, came saying Allah cursed wine, its presser, drinker, carrier, one to whom carried, seller, buyer, server and one served. > **""Allah has cursed wine, its presser, drinker, carrier, seller, buyer, server and one served.""**"
"8203","Khalid ibn Yazid, from Thabit ibn Zayd al-Khawlani, said he came to Madinah, met Ibn Abbas and asked about wine. Ibn Abbas said he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the mosque when he undid his cloak and ordered whoever had wine to inform him. People brought skins and jars, he ordered them gathered at such-and-such Baqi, walked leaning with Abu Bakr and Umar swapping sides, asked people do you know this, they said wine, and he declared Allah cursed wine, presser, drinker, server, carrier, seller, buyer and consumer of price. Then he called for a knife, had it sharpened, cut the skins, and when people noted their benefit, said yes but I do so in anger for Allah at His displeasure therein. > **""Do you know this. Allah has cursed wine, its presser, drinker, server, carrier, seller, buyer and consumer of its price. Sharpen it for me.""**"
"8204","Uthman ibn Abi al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed its drinker and seller, meaning wine. A fuller version came under the price of wine. > **""Allah has cursed its drinker and seller.""**"
"8205","Abu Awfa reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said none drinks wine while drinking it as a believer, nor fornicates while fornicating as a believer. The full report is in the chapter of faith. > **""None drinks wine while drinking it as a believer, nor fornicates while fornicating as a believer.""**"
"8206","Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said three do not enter Paradise: the wine addict, severer of kinship, and believer in magic; whoever dies addicted, Allah gives him nahr al-Ghutah, a river flowing from the sores of prostitutes harming Hell's people with the stench of their privates. > **""Three do not enter Paradise: the wine addict, severer of kinship, and believer in magic. Whoever dies addicted, Allah gives him nahr al-Ghutah.""**"
"8207","Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said five masters do not enter Paradise: the wine addict, believer in magic, severer of kinship, soothsayer and giver of reminders of charity. > **""Five do not enter Paradise: the wine addict, believer in magic, severer of kinship, soothsayer and giver of reminders.""**"
"8208","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the wine addict, disobedient to parents and giver of reminders do not enter the wall of Holiness, elsewhere Paradise of Firdaws and enclosure of Holiness. > **""The wine addict, disobedient to parents and giver of reminders do not enter the enclosure of Holiness.""**"
"8209","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever of his community dies drinking wine, Allah forbids him its drink in Paradise, and whoever dies wearing gold, Allah forbids him its wear in Paradise. > **""Whoever of my community dies drinking wine, Allah forbids him its drink in Paradise, and whoever dies wearing gold, Allah forbids him its wear in Paradise.""**"
"8210","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the wine addict, if he dies, meets Allah like an idol worshiper. > **""The wine addict, if he dies, meets Allah like an idol worshiper.""**"
"8211","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said no wine addict, disobedient or giver of reminders enters Paradise. Ibn Abbas found this hard, since believers sin, till he found it in Allah's Book: the disobedient in Muhammad 22, the giver in al-Baqarah 264, and wine in al-Maidah 90 till avoid it. > **""No wine addict, disobedient or giver of reminders enters Paradise.""**"
"8212","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say dwelling upon wine is like worship of idols. > **""Dwelling upon wine is like worship of idols.""**"
"8213","Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say no wine addict, giver of reminders for deeds, or disobedient to parents enters Paradise. > **""No wine addict, giver of reminders for deeds, or disobedient to parents enters Paradise.""**"
"8214","Jafar ibn Sulayman said he visited Farqad alone and asked about his reports of sinking and stoning, whether his own words or from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Farqad traced it through Asim al-Bajali from Abu Umamah, Qatadah from Said ibn al-Musayyib, and Ibrahim al-Nakhai: a group of his community sleeps over eating, drinking, play and amusement, mornings as monkeys and pigs, wind wipes a tribe as before, for permitting wine, beating drums and taking singers. > **""A group of my community sleeps over eating, drinking, play and amusement, then mornings as monkeys and pigs, for permitting wine, beating drums and taking singers.""**"
"8215","Farqad al-Sabikhi traced through Abu Munib from Abu Ata from Ubadah, Shahr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, Asim from Abu Umamah, and Said or Ibn Abbas: by Him in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, people of his community sleep over evil, pride, play and amusement, mornings as monkeys and pigs, for permitting prohibitions, taking singers, drinking wine, eating usury and wearing silk. > **""By Him in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, people of my community sleep over evil and amusement, then mornings as monkeys and pigs, for permitting prohibitions, taking singers, drinking wine, eating usury and wearing silk.""**"
"8216","Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said a group of his community will permit wine under a name they give it. > **""A group of my community will permit wine under a name they give it.""**"
"8217","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever wishes Allah to give him wine in the Hereafter, let him leave it in this world, and whoever wishes Allah to clothe him silk in the Hereafter, let him leave it in this world. > **""Whoever wishes Allah to give him wine in the Hereafter, let him leave it in this world, and whoever wishes Allah to clothe him silk in the Hereafter, let him leave it in this world.""**"
"8218","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever leaves wine while able, I shall give him drink from the enclosure of Holiness, and whoever leaves silk while able, I shall clothe him from the enclosure of Holiness. > **""Whoever leaves wine while able, I shall give him drink from the enclosure of Holiness, and whoever leaves silk while able, I shall clothe him from the enclosure of Holiness.""**"
"8219","Abu Shaykh al-Hunai reported that Muawiyah asked Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whether they knew the Messenger of Allah forbade drinking in gold and silver vessels, and they said yes."
"8220","In another narration, Abu Shaykh was among Companions when Muawiyah adjured them by Allah whether the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade drinking in silver vessels. They said yes by Allah, and Muawiyah said and I bear witness."
"8221","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only forbade drinking in silver vessels. He added the Prophet only forbade solid silk; if warp or weft alone is silk, no harm in wearing it."
"8222","Kulthum ibn Jabr said they were at Wasit with Abd al-Ala when a man called Abu al-Ghadiyah asked for water, was brought a silvered vessel, refused to drink, and recalled the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then mentioned the report."
"8223","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks in gold and silver vessels only gargles Hellfire in his belly. > **""Whoever drinks in gold and silver vessels only gargles Hellfire in his belly.""**"
"8224","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks in a gold vessel or silver vessel only gargles Hellfire in his belly. > **""Whoever drinks in a gold vessel or a silver vessel only gargles Hellfire in his belly.""**"
"8225","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever wears silk and drinks in silver is not of us, and whoever sows discord between a woman and her husband, or a slave and his masters, is not of us. > **""Whoever wears silk and drinks in silver is not of us, and whoever sows discord between a woman and her husband, or a slave and his masters, is not of us.""**"
"8226","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade him to drink in a vessel of silver. > **""Do not drink in a vessel of silver.""**"
"8227","Umm Salamah and Hafsah, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said whoever drinks in a silver vessel gargles Hellfire in his belly. The report of Umm Salamah is in the Sahih. > **""Whoever drinks in a silver vessel gargles Hellfire in his belly.""**"
"8228","Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a drinking vessel of gold, then he mentioned the report."
"8229","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said al-Muqawqis gifted the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a cup of glass, in which he used to drink. Ibn Majah reported it briefly."
"8230","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, said Muadh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, had a cup plated with copper, in which he gave the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink, and with which he poured ablution water for him."
"8231","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade bending the mouths of waterskins to drink. > **""Do not bend the mouths of waterskins to drink.""**"
"8232","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said he forbade drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. > **""Do not drink from the mouth of the waterskin.""**"
"8233","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said he forbade drinking from the crack of the cup. > **""Do not drink from the crack of the cup.""**"
"8234","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said he permitted drinking from the mouths of leather water bags. The report of Umm Sulaym on drinking standing will come."
"8235","Sahl ibn Sad, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade blowing into drink, and drinking from the cracked side of the cup or its handle. > **""Do not blow into drink, and do not drink from the cracked side of the cup or its handle.""**"
"8236","Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, said it is disliked to drink from the cracked side of the cup and the handle of the cup."
"8237","Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left them in no confusion about religion, forbidding blowing into drink. > **""Do not blow into drink.""**"
"8238","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, disliked blowing before him in prayer or in his drink. Reports on blowing over food came earlier."
"8239","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade blowing over food, drink and dates. Abu Dawud reported it without the words dates. > **""Do not blow over food, drink or dates.""**"
"8240","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked which drink is best, and said the sweet cold. > **""The sweet cold drink.""**"
"8241","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man drinking standing and said vomit it up. Asked why, he said would it please you for a cat to drink with you. He said no, and the Prophet said one worse than it drank with you: Satan. > **""Vomit it up. Would it please you for a cat to drink with you. One worse than it drank with you: Satan.""**"
"8242","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said if one who drinks standing knew what is in his belly, he would vomit it up. He has a report in the Sahih with another wording. > **""If one who drinks standing knew what is in his belly, he would vomit it up.""**"
"8243","Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, said he forbade a man to drink standing. > **""Do not drink standing.""**"
"8244","Zadhan reported that Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, drank standing, people looked as if disapproving, and he said why do they stare. If I drink standing, I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink standing, and if I drink sitting, I saw him drink sitting. Only drinking standing is in the Sahih."
"8245","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon an Ansari woman, in the house a hanging skin, bent its mouth and drank standing."
"8246","Umm Sulaym, may Allah be pleased with her, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her, in her house a hanging skin, drank from it standing, and she cut off the mouth of the skin."
"8247","Muslim said he asked Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, about drinking standing. He said, nephew, I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hobble his kneeling mount holding its rein with foot on its foreleg, when Quraysh gathered round, he was brought milk, drank mounted, then passed to his right, and all drank standing."
"8248","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank standing, elsewhere milk, and elsewhere entered their mosque and drank standing."
"8249","Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, said he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink standing."
"8250","Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them, said he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink standing."
"8251","Said ibn Jubayr said Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, told him he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink Zamzam standing."
"8252","Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, said she saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink standing and sitting."
"8253","A man of Juhaynah said he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say the disbeliever drinks with seven intestines and the believer drinks with one intestine. > **""The disbeliever drinks with seven intestines and the believer drinks with one intestine.""**"
"8254","Nadlah ibn Amr al-Ghifari said he met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at two watering places with milch camels, gave him drink, then drank the leftover and was filled, though before he drank seven without fullness. The Prophet said the believer drinks with one intestine and the disbeliever with seven. > **""The believer drinks with one intestine and the disbeliever drinks with seven intestines.""**"
"8255","Bahz reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, brushed teeth sideways, drank by sipping, breathed three times, and said it is more wholesome, pleasant and healing. > **""It is more wholesome, pleasant and healing.""**"
"8256","Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when fasting began with drink, without gulping, drinking twice or thrice."
"8257","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to drink in three breaths."
"8258","Abdullah said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, breathed in the vessel three times, naming Allah with each breath and thanking at the last of them."
"8259","Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drank in three breaths. When he brought the vessel to his mouth he named Allah, when he lowered it he praised Allah, doing that three times."
"8260","Nawfal ibn Muawiyah al-Dayli said he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink in three breaths, naming Allah in the first and praising Him in the last."
"8261","Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, reported that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, breathed in the vessel three times."
"8262","Jarir said Uyaynah ibn Hisn entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a man present, asked for drink, was given water screened, drank, and asked what this is. He said modesty and faith were given to them and withheld from you. > **""Modesty and faith were given to them and withheld from you.""**"
"8263","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave drink he said begin with the eldest, or the elders. > **""Begin with the eldest.""**"
"8264","Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with Abu Bakr, Umar, Abu Ubaydah and others, was brought a cup, offered it to Abu Ubaydah, who said you deserve it first. He said take it, and before drinking Abu Ubaydah offered it back, so the Prophet said drink, for blessing is with our elders, and whoever shows no mercy to our young nor honor to our elder is not of us. > **""Drink, for blessing is with our elders. Whoever shows no mercy to our young nor honor to our elder is not of us.""**"
"8265","Abdullah ibn Abi Habibah, asked what he remembered of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said he came to their mosque at Quba, he came as a young boy sat on his right with Abu Bakr on his left, then the Prophet called for drink, drank, and passed to him on his right."
"8266","Abdullah ibn Busr, from his father Busr, reported that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came riding a Syrian mule called donkey, entered with Companions, his mother laid a velvet cloth on a mat perfuming it, his father offered dates, his mother cooked porridge, Abdullah served, they ate, then he gave them fadikh to drink. The Prophet drank, gave to his right, when the cup emptied Abdullah refilled and was told to give where the cup had reached. After food the Prophet prayed forgiveness, mercy and blessed provision for them, whose plenty they still knew. Part is in the Sahih from Abdullah himself, this from his father. > **""Give it to where the cup had reached. O Allah, forgive them, have mercy on them, and bless them in their provision.""**"
"8267","Abdullah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with them, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to them, his grandmother offered dates, cooked food, they gave drink, the cup emptied, he brought another as servant, and the Prophet said give the cup where it had reached. He has another report in the Sahih. > **""Give the cup where it had reached.""**"
"8268","Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with him, said on a journey they found no water, then came upon water after. They gave the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, drink, and each time he said the server drinks last, three times, till all drank. Abu Dawud reported only the words server drinks last. > **""The server drinks last.""**"
"8269","In another narration, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were thirsty, he halted, was brought a vessel, began watering them while they said drink, and he said likewise. > **""The server drinks last.""**"
"8270","Al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said the server drinks last. > **""The server drinks last.""**"
"8271","Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, halted, a woman sent a ewe with her son, he milked and said take it to your mother, and she drank her fill. Then another ewe, he milked and gave Abu Bakr, then another, milked and drank himself."
"8272","Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to their house, he handed him a bucket, he drank, then rinsed his mouth into the bucket."
"8273","Ibn Abi Shaykh said the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to them saying, O Muharib, may Allah brighten you, do not give me milk of a woman to drink. > **""O Muharib, may Allah brighten you, do not give me milk of a woman to drink.""**"
"8274","Jabir and Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them, reported that a man called Abu Humayd brought the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a vessel of milk from al-Naqi by day, and the Prophet said why did you not cover it, even with a stick across it. The report of Jabir is in the Sahih. Similar reports on manners will come. > **""Why did you not cover it, even with a stick across it.""**"
